                    },
                    "message": "What does this have to do with the unit files being a library or not?  I'm not really following."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "If we don't make a library for entity-manager, we need to compile some .cpp files multiple times.\n\nThis is how it currently looks like on master\n\n```\n\ntest(\n    'test_entity_manager',\n    executable(\n        'test_entity_manager',\n        'test_entity-manager.cpp',\n        '../src/entity_manager/expression.cpp',\n        '../src/utils.cpp',\n        '../src/entity_manager/utils.cpp',\n        cpp_args: test_boost_args,\n        dependencies: [\n            boost,\n            gtest,\n            nlohmann_json_dep,\n            phosphor_logging_dep,\n            sdbusplus,\n            valijson,\n        ],\n        include_directories: test_include_dir,\n    ),  \n)\n```\n\nSo a bunch of files are listed there which were already compiled for entity-manager. So no need to compile it again here."
                },
